---
title: States of the Aggregation Service - CAS Beacon and SMT Beacon cohorts
---

%% One state machine for the Aggregation Service.
%% It follows the RECOMMENDED MuSig2 example of the specification.
%% The service sees hashes only. It never needs a DID document or a BTCR2 Update.

stateDiagram-v2
    state "Cohort defined: Beacon Type (CAS or SMT),<br/>size, costs, timing, pull or push flow" as Defined
    state "Advertised (for example Nostr or DIDComm)" as Advertised
    state "Enrolling: collect did or didIndex<br/>and a Schnorr public key per participant" as Enrolling
    state "Finalized: compute the n-of-n P2TR Beacon Address,<br/>send it with the n public keys" as Finalized
    state "Active cohort" as Active {
        state "Ready for a round" as Ready
        state "Collect responses: update or no update,<br/>and a MuSig2 nonce, from all n participants" as Collect
        state "Build the Beacon Signal:<br/>CAS: CAS Announcement, Signal Bytes = its hash<br/>SMT: optimized SMT, Signal Bytes = root, SMT Proofs<br/>Unsigned Beacon Signal, aggregated nonce" as Build
        state "Request confirmation: send the CAS Announcement<br/>or the SMT Proofs of each participant" as Request
        state "Collect partial signatures from all n participants" as Sign
        state "Aggregate the partial signatures, broadcast" as Broadcast
        state "Round failed: discard the nonces" as Failed

        [*] --> Ready
        Ready --> Collect: announce an update opportunity (pull),<br/>or first update received (push)
        Collect --> Build: all n responses
        Collect --> Failed: a participant does not respond
        Build --> Request
        Request --> Sign
        Sign --> Broadcast: all n partial signatures
        Sign --> Failed: a participant refuses or does not respond
        Broadcast --> Ready: Beacon Signal broadcast
        Failed --> Ready: next round with new MuSig2 nonces
    }
    state "Cohort closed" as Closed

    [*] --> Defined
    Defined --> Advertised
    Advertised --> Enrolling
    Enrolling --> Enrolling: participant enrolls
    Enrolling --> Finalized: membership closed
    Finalized --> Active: participants verified the address
    Active --> Closed: participants leave, or the service stops
    Closed --> [*]
